      "spam": false,
      "value": "lower end GPUs like the GTX 960? \nRecommended min spec is still a 970 for VR. So why should a small team like the VRC crew support hardware that was never meant to be used for VR and is outdated by now anyway? \nIf you think the card is too slow, upgrade the hardware instead of nagging others to solve your problem. (I know it costs money)\n\nBUT! in most cases it is the CPU not GFX card that struggles with all the drawcalls and the overhead from all the player IK and audio stuff. My gtx980ti shows an average usage of 50-80% and my i7 is glowing red cause it has to do all the hard work alone. A lot of the worlds are console rips or from older games anyway so even the weakest supported GFX hardware should be subchallenged most of the time.",
      "viewerReactions": null
    },
